<title>JAPAN: No step needed if dlr tops 120 yen-Ex-MOF official.</title>
<headline>No step needed if dlr tops 120 yen-Ex-MOF official.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese and U.S. monetary authorities do not need to take steps even if the dollar rises above 120 yen, Tomomitsu Oba, head of the Japan Center for International Finance and a former vice finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters Financial Television on Thursday.</p>
</text>
